      <h3>Essential Safety Protocols in Aerosol Manufacturing</h3>

      <ul>
        <li>Hazardous area zoning and explosion-proof electrical systems</li>
        <li>Gas detection and automatic emergency shut-off</li>
        <li>Grounding and bonding against static electricity</li>
        <li>Foam-based and dry chemical fire suppression</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Navigating Global Regulations</h3>

      <p>Modern compliance frameworks include UN and DOT transport rules, GHS labeling, VOC emission limits, and national fire and explosives regulations. Regulations evolved after the phase-out of CFC propellants under the Montreal Protocol and continue to emphasize environmental and occupational safety.</p>

      <h3>Pressure Testing and Container Integrity Requirements</h3>

      <ul>
        <li>Hydrostatic burst testing of containers</li>
        <li>Pressure retention testing over shelf life</li>
        <li>Leak testing using hot water bath and gas sniffers</li>
        <li>Drop and mechanical impact testing</li>
      </ul>

